# Shell scripts MUST be LF. Bash on macOS/Linux treats CR as part of
# the next token (variable names, etc.), which breaks scripts in
# subtle, hard-to-diagnose ways. PowerShell tolerates both, but we
# pin .ps1 to LF too for consistency.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=lf

# Other text files follow git's default (line-endings normalised on
# commit, native on checkout) unless explicitly overridden.
*.md    text
LICENSE text
